NAME
       runlevel - print the old and current SysV runlevel

SYNOPSIS
       runlevel

DESCRIPTION
       runlevel prints two values: the previous runlevel (N when there was
       none) and the current one. Runlevels are the older names for systemd
       targets, kept for compatibility: 3 is multi-user.target (text mode), 5
       graphical.target, 1 rescue.target, 0 poweroff and 6 reboot.

       On RHEL 9, work with targets instead: systemctl get-default, systemctl
       set-default, systemctl isolate.

EXAMPLES
           runlevel
           systemctl get-default

SEE ALSO
       systemctl(1), systemd.special(7)
